# Ramallah Memory Atlas — ignore rules
#
# CLAUDE.md §6: ".env* git-ignored from commit #1." That rule is absolute here —
# there is deliberately no `!.env.example` negation, because a negation is a hole
# and this project has already paid for one leaked credential. A committed
# template belongs at `env.example` (no leading dot), which these rules allow
# through while every real `.env…` stays out.

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.env
.envrc

# Edge Function local secrets. A DIFFERENT filename from `.env`, so not one of the
# rules above touches it — and it is precisely where TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY and a
# service-role key land the moment Edge Function work starts (M1). Committed, it
# would be world-readable: the Pages origin serves dotfiles today (`/.gitignore`
# and `/.gitleaks.toml` both return 200).
#
# No leading slash, so a pattern matches at EVERY depth. `.dev.vars` alone already
# covers `supabase/.dev.vars` and `supabase/functions/.dev.vars`; the second line
# catches the `.dev.vars.local` variant. Verified with `git check-ignore -v` rather
# than assumed — the same reason scripts/forbidden-paths.ere carries the twin rule
# for the force-added case.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Anything that smells like a key. Belt and braces alongside gitleaks.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
service-role*
*service_role*
secrets.json
.secrets/

# ── Supabase CLI ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local stack state and generated temp files. Migrations, config.toml,
# functions and tests are all tracked — only runtime state is ignored.
.supabase/
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
supabase/logs/

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/
.node_repl_history

# ── Build & tooling output ───────────────────────────────────
dist/
.cache/
coverage/
gitleaks-report.json
*.log

# ── Cloudflare ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.wrangler/

# ── Bootstrapped tooling ─────────────────────────────────────
# The pinned gitleaks binary fetched by scripts/install-gitleaks.ps1. The VERSION is
# tracked (in that script and in the CI workflow); the binary is not.
.tools/

# ── Editors & OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Real footage for the timing probe. NEVER committed — 1.2 GB, and ladder-fixture.ts
# refuses committed real footage on purpose. Staged locally, read by probe-timing.ts.
fottage/

# ── Basemap archives ─────────────────────────────────────────
# A Palestine extract is ~180 MB. It belongs in the R2 `public` bucket, which is what
# scripts/provision-basemap.ts puts it there for, and its identity in this repository is
# one line of config/site.json. Never the bytes.
*.pmtiles
